    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "Batch (file batch.go)", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "retained_via_interfaces named the abstraction and carrier but not the runtime INJECTION site; I had to grep/read db.go:1436, db.go:1312/1377, db.go:908/950->failover_writer.go:179/259, compaction_scheduler.go:304, bench/ycsb.go:316 to prove which satisfier the interface field actually holds"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "Batch (file batch.go)", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "no way to distinguish a real injection from a mere interface-satisfaction candidate (compact.Iter, record.Writer.flusher), so I had to grep internal/compact/ to refute them"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "Batch (file batch.go)", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "goroutine-crossing evidence for the risk ranking — I grepped for 'go s.periodicGranter' (compaction_scheduler.go:306) and 'wg.Go' (bench/ycsb.go:327) since the graph carries no go-statement/concurrency edges"}
  ],
  "q3_hints": [],
  "q4_value": "The retained_via_interfaces field on sense_blast: it enumerated interface-laundered Batch retainers with a declared containment chain (e.g. rangeKeyMasking > Iterator > iteratorBatchState > Batch, and batchIter behind InternalIterator) that a field-type sweep or grep for 'Batch' fundamentally cannot surface — exactly the treacherous class the audit was scoped to find.",
  "q5_improve": "For each retained_via_interfaces row, include the actual construction/injection site(s) where the field is assigned a concrete value (e.g. db.go:1436 for mergingIterLevel.iter), or a confidence flag distinguishing a verified assignment from a bare interface-satisfaction guess — that is precisely the grep work I had to do to confirm or refute every row.",
  "score": 9,
  "score_rationale": "Per Q1/Q4, retained_via_interfaces handed me transitive interface-laundered retention chains (batchIter behind InternalIterator, rangeKeyMasking behind SpanMask) I could not have recovered with grep/read in this session, and even the two false positives in Q1_wrong were cheap to refute — the fallbacks in Q2 were confirmation of injection sites, not rediscovery of the retainers."
}

